            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 1)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "5627dc6e-c943-439e-ab4a-4531b7f24264"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Beginning of Reconciliation</strong><br>\nReconciliation after conflicts is a first step toward peaceful coexistence. Various groups recognize the need to leave the past behind and build a shared future. In many cases, reconciliation begins with conversations and mutual understanding of the experiences and feelings of others.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Coexistence Initiatives Worldwide</strong><br>\nThere are many examples of successful coexistence initiatives worldwide. These initiatives promote dialogue and collaboration between former enemies. For instance, the peace initiative in Northern Ireland brought together former paramilitary fighters to collectively work on a peaceful solution.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Community Building</strong><br>\nCommunity building is at the forefront of many successful coexistence initiatives. Through joint projects and activities, participants learn to rebuild trust in one another. This lays the foundation for lasting peaceful coexistence and a positive shared future.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Educational Programs</strong><br>\nEducational programs are an essential part of coexistence initiatives. They help to break down prejudices and promote understanding of the culture and history of the other. Education also provides a platform for dialogue and discussion about the past and how to move forward together.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Cooperation</strong><br>\nEconomic cooperation can also be a path to promoting coexistence. Shared economic interests can bring groups together and lay the groundwork for sustainable reconciliation. For example, joint market projects or trade agreements can strengthen relationships between former enemies.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Social Media and Communication</strong><br>\nSocial media and other communication technologies play a significant role in spreading messages of reconciliation and coexistence. They offer platforms for dialogue and interaction between different groups, encourage understanding, and help identify common goals.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
